        <mxCell id="-aGxGEo2_JWixX-oLaSN-13" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Identifying service capacity and performance requirements&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Agreeing service capacity and performance requirements&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Determining capacity and performance measurement requirements&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Designing capacity and performance metrics and reports&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;The purpose of the capacity and performance management practice is to ensure that services achieve the agreed and expected levels of performance and satisfy current and future demand in a const-effective way.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects identify, manage and report service capacity and performance requirements, in order to maintain an adequate level of service quality.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: Capacity and Performance management (3.2.2)&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="-aGxGEo2_JWixX-oLaSN-12" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
