        <mxCell id="jNRMRp2S-dL0ja43aLe--2" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Change registration&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Change assessment&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Change authorization&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Change planning&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Change realization control&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Change review and closure&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;The purpose of the change enablement practice is to maximize the number of successful service and product changes by ensuring the risks have been properly assessed, authorizing changes to proceed, and managing the change schedule.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to manage changes within the project or in a DevOps environment diligently, in order to properly address the risk of changes and ensure the necessary service quality.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: Change enablement (3.2.2)&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="jNRMRp2S-dL0ja43aLe--1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
