        <mxCell id="s-qbUJ5rrHLjZnUm8olo-2" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Defining the objective of monitoring&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Assessing measurements available and criteria to be monitored&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Defining types of events for the object of monitoring&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Defining the thresholds for different type of events&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Defining a service &#39;health model (end-to-end events)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Defining events correlations and rule sets&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Mapping events with action plans and functions responsible and notified&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;The purpose of the monitoring and event management practice is to systematically observe services and services components, and record and report selected changes of state identified as events.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to set up a central monitoring for the projects IT infrastructure, in order to collect all logs and enable the enterprise to detect events.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: Monitoring and event management&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;(3.2.2)&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="s-qbUJ5rrHLjZnUm8olo-1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
