        <mxCell id="DO11c-6wLbNFiMZy8dLW-2" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Product architecture and service relationship analysis&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Release management approach review and development&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Release management model&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Release instance planning&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Release plan communication&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;The purpose of the release management practice is to make new and changed services and features available for use.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to plan their releases according to the enterprises strategy, in order to maintain a common approach and plannable way of releasing new functionalities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: Release management (3.2.2)&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="DO11c-6wLbNFiMZy8dLW-1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
